I now have all the information needed. Let me compile the complete implementation plan.

---

## Implementation Plan: GNB Hover Rect Indicator

### Architecture Overview

The feature requires coordinated changes across three files. The critical design decisions, resolved before the step-by-step plan:

**Gap value between rect and label:** The `__gnb-link` already declares `gap: var(--gutter-sm)` as its flex gap. Because the rect will be `position: absolute` (pulled out of flow), the flex gap no longer applies to it. The JS translateX offset must therefore read `getComputedStyle(linkEl).gap` at first hover rather than burning a hardcoded constant — this keeps it responsive to the fluid `--gutter-sm` value (14px–20px range) without a resize listener. Cache the parsed value per-link and re-read it on each `mouseenter` (one `getComputedStyle` call per hover is negligible; avoids a resize subscription entirely).

**Label translateX vs rect animation:** Animate both elements in the same `gsap.to()` call passing an array target `[rectEl, labelEl]` with separate property vars, OR use two concurrent `gsap.to()` calls that share the same duration/ease. The cleaner approach — matching the project's `CharBtn` pattern — is two separate `gsap.to()` calls with identical duration and ease, no timeline needed. This avoids coupling the elements to a single tween reference while keeping the motion perfectly synchronized.

**Resize handling:** Re-measure `getBoundingClientRect().width` on every `mouseenter` (not cached from init). The rect is tiny (~6-10px), so the measurement is trivial. This handles viewport resize and font-size changes without a `ResizeObserver` or window resize listener.

---

### Step 1 — PHP: `views/components/drawer.php`

Two insertion points, both adding the same `<span>` fragment BEFORE `<span class="no-drawer__gnb-label">`.

**Insertion 1 — "With sub" variant (current line 78):**

Current:
```php
<span class="no-drawer__gnb-label"><?= e($label) ?></span>
```

Becomes (insert the rect span on the line immediately before):
```php
<span class="no-loop-filter-rect no-drawer__gnb-rect" aria-hidden="true"><span></span><span></span><span></span><span></span></span>
<span class="no-drawer__gnb-label"><?= e($label) ?></span>
```

Specifically, the full `<a>` block at lines 75–79 becomes:
```php
<a href="<?= e($href) ?>"
    class="no-drawer__gnb-link wavy-link f-display-0<?= $isActive ? ' is-active' : '' ?>"
    <?= !empty($target) ? ' target="' . e($target) . '"' : '' ?>>
    <span class="no-loop-filter-rect no-drawer__gnb-rect" aria-hidden="true"><span></span><span></span><span></span><span></span></span>
    <span class="no-drawer__gnb-label"><?= e($label) ?></span>
</a>
```

**Insertion 2 — "Without sub" variant (current line 97):**

Current:
```php
<span class="no-drawer__gnb-label"><?= e($label) ?></span>
```

Becomes (line 96–98):
```php
<a href="<?= e($href) ?>"
    class="no-drawer__gnb-link wavy-link f-display-0<?= $isActive ? ' is-active' : '' ?>"
    <?= !empty($target) ? ' target="' . e($target) . '"' : '' ?><?= ($target === '_blank') ? ' rel="noopener noreferrer"' : '' ?>>
    <span class="no-loop-filter-rect no-drawer__gnb-rect" aria-hidden="true"><span></span><span></span><span></span><span></span></span>
    <span class="no-drawer__gnb-label"><?= e($label) ?></span>
</a>
```

**Key point:** No `aria-label` or semantic role changes — the rect is `aria-hidden="true"` on a `<span>`, which is already established by the badge rect at lines 103–108 of the same file.

---

### Step 2 — SCSS: `resource/scss/layouts/_drawer.scss`

Insert a new `&__gnb-rect` block immediately after the existing `&__gnb-link` block (after line 282, before line 284 which is the `.masking-text` comment).

```scss
  &__gnb-rect {
    position: absolute;
    left: 0;
    top: 50%;
    // Vertical centering is owned by GSAP (yPercent: -50).
    // DO NOT use CSS transform here — GSAP will overwrite it.
    pointer-events: none;
    // Initially invisible; GSAP sets opacity: 0, scale: 0.5 on mount.
    // opacity: 0 is set inline by JS — no need for CSS here, but
    // keeping visibility: hidden as a non-GSAP-conflicting fallback
    // would conflict with the scale origin. Leave to GSAP only.
  }
```

However there is a real structural concern: the `__gnb-link` has `display: inline-flex` with `gap: var(--gutter-sm)`. Once the rect is `position: absolute`, it is removed from flow and the flex gap no longer pushes the label right — GSAP translateX on the label achieves this instead.

The `__gnb-link` already has `position: relative`, so the absolute child positions correctly within it.

One important detail: the `__gnb-link` currently has `padding: var(--gutter-sm) 0`. The absolute rect at `left: 0; top: 50%` will overlap the padding area. Since the rect is tiny (~6-10px wide), this is visually fine.

The complete SCSS addition after line 282:

```scss
  // GNB hover rect indicator — absolutely positioned, GSAP-owned transforms
  &__gnb-rect {
    position: absolute;
    left: 0;
    top: 50%;
    // yPercent: -50 applied by GSAP for true vertical centering
    // No CSS transform — GSAP owns all transforms on this element
    pointer-events: none;
    // opacity and scale are set to initial hidden state by GSAP on mount
  }
```

No `will-change`, no CSS `opacity: 0` — GSAP's `set()` call during `_initGnbRects` initializes the hidden state on mount so there is no flash.

---

### Step 3 — TypeScript Config: `resource/ts/config/component.config.ts`

Add a new exported const block for the rect animation parameters. Per project rules, no magic numbers in TS. Insert after the `DRAWER_CLASSES` block (after line 492):

```typescript
export const DRAWER_GNB_RECT = {
  /** CSS selector for the rect indicator inside each gnb-link */
  rectSelector: ".no-drawer__gnb-rect",
  /** CSS selector for the label text span inside each gnb-link */
  labelSelector: ".no-drawer__gnb-label",
  /** GSAP initial hidden state */
  initOpacity: 0,
  initScale: 0.5,
  transformOrigin: "left center",
  /** Hover-in animation */
  enterDuration: 0.38,
  enterEase: "power3.out",
  /** Hover-out animation */
  leaveDuration: 0.26,
  leaveEase: "power2.in",
} as const;
```

The selectors belong here rather than in `dom.config.ts` because they are animation-specific sub-element selectors, not top-level DOM configuration keys.

---

### Step 4 — TypeScript: `resource/ts/types/component.types.ts`

Add a new interface for the per-link binding record. Per project rules, all types go in `resource/ts/types/*.types.ts`. Append after the last export (after line 376):

```typescript
export interface GnbRectBinding {
  link: HTMLElement;
  rect: HTMLElement;
  label: HTMLElement;
  onEnter: EventListener;
  onLeave: EventListener;
}
```

---

### Step 5 — TypeScript: `resource/ts/ui/Drawer.ts`

This is the largest change. The full set of modifications:

**5a — Add import for new config constant** (after line 8 in the existing import block):

```typescript
import {
  MASKING_ANIM,
  DRAWER_ANIM,
  DRAWER_CLASSES,
  DRAWER_GNB_RECT,
} from "../config/component.config.js";
```

**5b — Add import for new type** (after the `MagneticCornerGsap` import, within the `component.types` import on lines 13–14):

```typescript
import type { MagneticCornerGsap, GnbRectBinding } from "../types/component.types.js";
```

**5c — Add private field** inside the `Drawer` class body, after line 39 (`private _magneticCorner`):

```typescript
private _gnbRectCleanups: Array<() => void> = [];
```

**5d — Call `_initGnbRects` from `mount()`** (after line 100, `this._mountMagneticCorner(root)`):

```typescript
this._initGnbRects(root);
```

**5e — Add the `_initGnbRects` private method** after the `_mountMagneticCorner` method (after line 121):

```typescript
private _initGnbRects(root: HTMLElement): void {
  const gsap = getGsap();
  if (!gsap) return;

  const links = Array.from(
    root.querySelectorAll<HTMLElement>(DOM_CONFIG.drawer.gnbLinkSelector),
  );

  for (const link of links) {
    const rectEl = link.querySelector<HTMLElement>(DRAWER_GNB_RECT.rectSelector);
    const labelEl = link.querySelector<HTMLElement>(DRAWER_GNB_RECT.labelSelector);
    if (!rectEl || !labelEl) continue;

    const isActive = link.classList.contains(DRAWER_CLASSES.linkActive);

    // Initialize GSAP state — always set regardless of active state
    gsap.set(rectEl, {
      opacity: DRAWER_GNB_RECT.initOpacity,
      scale: DRAWER_GNB_RECT.initScale,
      transformOrigin: DRAWER_GNB_RECT.transformOrigin,
      yPercent: -50,
    });
    gsap.set(labelEl, { x: 0 });

    if (isActive) {
      // Active link: show rect immediately, shift label synchronously
      const rectWidth = rectEl.getBoundingClientRect().width;
      const gap = this._readLinkGap(link);
      gsap.set(rectEl, { opacity: 1, scale: 1 });
      gsap.set(labelEl, { x: rectWidth + gap });
    }

    const onEnter = (): void => {
      const gsap = getGsap();
      if (!gsap) return;
      // Re-measure on each hover to handle viewport resize
      const rectWidth = rectEl.getBoundingClientRect().width;
      const gap = this._readLinkGap(link);
      gsap.killTweensOf?.([rectEl, labelEl]);
      gsap.to(rectEl, {
        opacity: 1,
        scale: 1,
        duration: DRAWER_GNB_RECT.enterDuration,
        ease: DRAWER_GNB_RECT.enterEase,
        overwrite: "auto",
      });
      gsap.to(labelEl, {
        x: rectWidth + gap,
        duration: DRAWER_GNB_RECT.enterDuration,
        ease: DRAWER_GNB_RECT.enterEase,
        overwrite: "auto",
      });
    };

    const onLeave = (): void => {
      // Do not animate out if the link is the active page
      if (link.classList.contains(DRAWER_CLASSES.linkActive)) return;
      const gsap = getGsap();
      if (!gsap) return;
      gsap.killTweensOf?.([rectEl, labelEl]);
      gsap.to(rectEl, {
        opacity: DRAWER_GNB_RECT.initOpacity,
        scale: DRAWER_GNB_RECT.initScale,
        duration: DRAWER_GNB_RECT.leaveDuration,
        ease: DRAWER_GNB_RECT.leaveEase,
        overwrite: "auto",
      });
      gsap.to(labelEl, {
        x: 0,
        duration: DRAWER_GNB_RECT.leaveDuration,
        ease: DRAWER_GNB_RECT.leaveEase,
        overwrite: "auto",
      });
    };

    link.addEventListener("mouseenter", onEnter);
    link.addEventListener("mouseleave", onLeave);

    this._gnbRectCleanups.push((): void => {
      link.removeEventListener("mouseenter", onEnter);
      link.removeEventListener("mouseleave", onLeave);
      const gsap = getGsap();
      if (gsap) {
        gsap.killTweensOf?.([rectEl, labelEl]);
        gsap.set(labelEl, { x: 0 });
        gsap.set(rectEl, { opacity: 0, scale: DRAWER_GNB_RECT.initScale });
      }
    });
  }
}

private _readLinkGap(link: HTMLElement): number {
  // Read the computed CSS gap from the flex link element.
  // gap is a shorthand; column-gap is what inline-flex uses for item spacing.
  const raw = window.getComputedStyle(link).columnGap;
  const parsed = parseFloat(raw);
  return Number.isFinite(parsed) ? parsed : 0;
}
